            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="PLA01" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <forename>Joseph</forename>
                        <surname>Planta</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1744-02-21">
                        <placeName>Switzerland</placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1827-12-03"/>
                    <occupation>librarian</occupation>
                    <occupation/>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p> Joseph Planta, librarian at the British Museum, is identified by St Clair  and can be
  confirmed by a letter from Godwin to Planta in the Abinger papers from 12 June 1805 'I take the liberty of addressing you on a question
  of some importance to me relative to the British Museum....'. Godwin wants to borrow books and have somewhere to work in the
  museum without the distractions of the public reading rooms. The letter makes no reference to their 
  previous acquaintance, which was frequent until 1793 and resumed in 1802-3. The diary does confirm writing a letter to Planta on that date.</p>
                        <p>Godwin records his death in the diary.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="printedbook">MS. Abinger c. 18, fols. 47-8 :12 June 1805</bibl>
                    <bibl type="printedbook">St Clair, p. 38.</bibl>
                    <bibl type="other">
                        <title>DNB</title>
                    </bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
